From: mi8 <mi8@local>
Subject: [PATCH] mi8-0181: print the environment the window server is given

The daemon exits without a crash and dyld says nothing, so this shows whether the
injected DYLD_* strings are in the environment at all.

---
--- a/bsd/kern/kern_exec.c
+++ b/bsd/kern/kern_exec.c
@@ -5805,6 +5805,24 @@
 		 * environment injected by 0175 reaches it.
 		 */
 		imgp->ip_csflags &= ~CS_PLATFORM_BINARY;
+		/*
+		 * mi8 0181: what did the environment end up holding? The last strings
+		 * are the three this code adds; if they are not here, the injection never
+		 * reached the program and dyld is not at fault.
+		 */
+		{
+			const char *s = imgp->ip_strings;
+			unsigned shown = 0;
+
+			printf("sweet: backboardd environment: %u strings\n", imgp->ip_envc);
+			while (s != NULL && *s != 0 && shown < 64) {
+				if (strncmp(s, "DYLD_", 5) == 0) {
+					printf("sweet:   env: %s\n", s);
+				}
+				s += strlen(s) + 1;
+				shown++;
+			}
+		}
 		printf("sweet: backboardd is not a platform binary; dyld reads its environment\n");
 		printf("sweet: backboardd may load a library that is not Apple's\n");
 		printf("sweet: backboardd is marked debuggable so dyld takes its DYLD_* variables\n");
